      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "unverified=['ogden']"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the 1987 film Moonstruck, Cher and Nicolas Cage’s characters met at the now‑closed Cammareri Brothers Bakery on Henry Street, a landmark for movie lovers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carroll_Gardens%2C_Brooklyn",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Carroll Gardens began as a 19th‑century enclave for Irish immigrants, later welcoming Norwegian settlers who built churches that still echo the area’s multicultural roots.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carroll_Gardens%2C_Brooklyn",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The neighborhood’s subway access is provided by the Carroll Street and Smith–Ninth Streets stations, which serve the F and G trains and connect residents to the rest of Brooklyn.",
